WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:16,160
I should debate whether to keep my colonoscopy schedule for 1125. I had several, I had scheduled several

00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:20,480
months ago when I was having GI issues with erratic bowel movements, twidges of my rectum,

00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:28,080
feeling like incomplete emptying and bloating issues have resolved, except some bloating still.

00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:36,720
I'm wondering if I'm just inviting issues. If I do the procedure,

00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:44,080
what are usual indications that you need to get one done? The only reason I am half inclined is

00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:54,880
because my back's insurance has been already paid. Also my CEA and CA2729 had those slight

00:00:54,880 --> 00:01:01,600
increases that I was told, that I told you about last week, but I don't know if that means anything.

00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:10,000
Okay, so why would a person want to get a colonoscopy? Of course, from a medical,

00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,640
and the medical answer that you get a colonoscopy to rule out any colon cancer, any polyps that are

00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:34,880
growing, any in pocketing of your colon, any inflammation in your colon, there's all sorts of

00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:41,200
things that will rule out and rule in and give diagnoses by doing a colonoscopy. So in that sense,

00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:46,000
they're great to do. Firstly, I've never had a colonoscopy and I don't feel like I'm ever going to

00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:51,200
get a colonoscopy. So is that the right thing to do? I can't say that's the right thing to do for

00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,080
everybody. We have patients, they may be listening to this, that we're diagnosed with cancer because

00:01:56,080 --> 00:02:02,640
they didn't root their routine colonoscopy. And if they didn't do it, they may have never caught it

00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:09,280
early enough. And it was a lifesaver for them. And we've had patients that regretted doing the

00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:15,760
colonoscopy. So it's really a difficult call. If you feel led to do the colonoscopy by all means that

00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:24,800
you should do it. If you feel like there's reasons for it. And from a medical standpoint,

00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:31,040
if I was a medical doctor, I would say the reason for doing a colonoscopy is that you're over 50,

00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:37,120
everybody over 50 is supposed to get a colonoscopy. Well, I'm over 60, I still haven't had a colonoscopy

00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:43,840
and I don't plan to do it, but that's just me. But I think there's benefits. You go to

00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:50,320
a good GI doctor and I don't think, you know, I know you hear some horror stories of,

00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:55,600
well, colonoscopy, I think that's like one of the hundred thousand or something. So I don't think

00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:59,600
you have to worry necessarily about that.

